Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a structured error frame with the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Streaming Error",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "status": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "The status code of the error.",
      "enum": [400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 415, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504]
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A human-readable description of the error."
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Additional details about the resume attempt, including the resume token and checkpoint cursor.",
      "properties": {
        "resume_token": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The resume token issued by the server during the initial resume attempt. This token should be included in subsequent resume attempts to allow the server to identify and continue the resume process from the appropriate checkpoint."
        },
        "checkpoint_cursor": {
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "The checkpoint cursor, which represents the position of the last successful checkpoint in the stream. This value can be used by the client to determine the point at which it should resume streaming from the server."
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
``
